# Fictional EP Tracklist

## 1. Open Sixth Rings Past the Missing Kick

**Story & Context:** The debut runs at 130 BPM. Lehua begins with a slack-key figure built from a thumbed low ANCHOR and a treble sixth. Marcus places one compact kick under the bass note, then removes the expected second kick while the open sixth continues into CARRY. The missing drum makes the ringing interval feel rhythmically active rather than merely sustained.

Noa answers the first CLEAR with one prepared-Wurlitzer suspended second. Malia replaces the next digital low-percussion hit with a hollow ipu-heke palm stroke. Evan remains silent until Lehua moves the melody upward, then adds one dry bass-trumpet fifth.

At the midpoint, Lehua deliberately shortens the CARRY by damping the open strings early. Marcus responds by bringing the sub in sooner, changing the perceived weight without altering tempo. The final cycle leaves the sixth ringing longer than expected; every scheduled percussion event waits until it disappears.

