## 2. Cargo Scale 19 Clears on the Late Snare

**Story & Context:** At 134 BPM, Marcus writes the EP’s most angular broken-beat pattern, with a late snare and two short kick doubles. Lehua plays alternating thumb bass beneath clipped upper voicings. Every fourth phrase she mutes the treble strings but allows one low open string to continue.

The late snare is permitted only after that surviving string reaches CLEAR. Noa places a dry Wurlitzer minor seventh immediately afterward, creating a three-stage sequence of guitar decay, snare, and fixed chord. Malia replaces alternating shaker positions with fingertip ipu-heke taps. Evan contributes short half-valve falls in the spaces between kick doubles.

In the last minute, Marcus keeps the snare timing fixed while Lehua changes the duration of her CARRY states. The snare therefore feels alternately late, perfectly placed, or almost early even though the machine has not moved.

